---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import { siteConfig } from '../data/site';
---

<BaseLayout
  title={`About | ${siteConfig.name}`}
  description="Learn how the site is designed for speed, search traffic, and ad-supported utility pages."
>
  <section class="hero">
    <p class="eyebrow">About the site</p>
    <h1>Built for speed, clarity, and repeat visits.</h1>
    <p class="lead">
      Toolshack is a utility site built around search intent. Every page answers one small task as
      quickly as possible, with minimal JavaScript and a layout that stays readable on mobile.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section class="section card-grid">
    <article class="content-card">
      <h2>Why this format works</h2>
      <p>
        Utility pages tend to rank when they are fast, specific, and easy to understand from the
        search results page. That is why each tool gets its own landing page.
      </p>
    </article>
    <article class="content-card">
      <h2>How ads fit in</h2>
      <p>
        Ad placements are kept separate from the tool logic, which lets you turn them on after
        policy pages and content depth are in place.
      </p>
    </article>
    <article class="content-card">
      <h2>What comes next</h2>
      <p>
        Add more tools in the same pattern: one intent, one page, one fast interaction, and one
        clear internal link back to the hub.
      </p>
    </article>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
